in an urgent push for diplomacy the  american president issued a stark  warning and a plea for peace to the  citizens of russia  you are not our enemy  and i do not believe you want a bloody  destructive war against ukraine  it came on a day of more mixed messages  from russia  the kremlin said it planned to pull back  some troops from border areas russia's  parliament requested vladimir putin  recognize russian-backed separatist  regions in ukraine  as independent states  and after a meeting with the german  chancellor putin made unsupported claims  of genocide in ukraine's donbass region  do we want war of course not he said so  far  we have not seen any sign of  de-escalation on the ground  true or not analysts see hopeful signs  in russia's claims of a modest troop  pullback i take it as a step back and i  take it as a hopeful sign again very  cautiously that he's prepared to step  away and negotiate some of the  issues  ukraine now surrounded on three sides by  150 000 russian troops sees less reason  for optimism an apparent cyber attack  hit several banks and government  websites tuesday  while back in washington the tone of the  american president suggested serious  concern that putin may not be talked  down let there be no doubt  if russia commits this breach by  invading ukraine  responsible nations around the world  will not hesitate to respond  tonight ukraine has made an emergency  request to nato for supplies to prepare  for what it calls large-scale crises  affecting its civilian population among  the items they're seeking demining  equipment explosives detection equipment  and medical supplies all ominous signs  of what may be to come  donna  jackson proskow in washington
 

